<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bali Strait</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> Strait is the narrow channel, only about 2.4 kilometres wide at its narrowest, that separates eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> from Bali in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> and links the Bali Sea with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. Ferries cross it between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ketapang">Ketapang</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banyuwangi">Banyuwangi</a> and Gilimanuk on Bali. It has long been a route for trade and migration between the two islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bali-strait.jpg" alt="Bali Strait" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Codobai · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bali_Strait_(Selat_Bali).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
